# photic_antiphase_40hz.ledc — documentation example, ~15 min
# Luminance-flat ("invisible") 40 Hz photic flicker, plus a 40 Hz audio click.
#
# Two complementary-colour banks run at the same rate 180 degrees apart:
#   mask 10 (the WARM bits of both zones) amber, phase 0
#   mask 5  (the COOL bits of both zones) blue,  phase 180
# Their luminances are matched, so the SUM is nearly constant and the flicker is
# hard to see, while each retinal location still receives a full 40 Hz
# oscillation. Measured on hardware: the fundamental cancels by 25.8 dB at a
# sensor that sees both banks equally, at a relative phase of 178.1 degrees
# against a commanded 180.
#
# `phase` is a LEAD, not a lag — the firmware ADDS phase*period/360 to elapsed
# time, so the edge arrives earlier. 0 and 180 are symmetric under negation, so
# an antiphase pair is the one case where the convention does not matter.
#
# Which physical pixels mask 10 and mask 5 reach depends entirely on
# CONFIG_LED_CHANNEL_MAP. The two banks must be physically INTERLEAVED for the
# cancellation to work in the eye; on a non-interleaved strip this degrades to
# two dim 40 Hz zones (still safe, just not invisible).
#
# SAFETY: not a medical device. Do not use if you have photosensitive epilepsy,
# a seizure disorder or a history of photic migraine; never while driving.
# 40 Hz is ABOVE the 15-25 Hz photosensitive band, brightness is capped at 20%,
# the 50% duty keeps a luminance floor (no black<->white contrast), the light
# ramps in over 15 s and out over 30 s, and the colours are amber and blue —
# never a saturated-red strobe.
#
# LED   : time freq duty bright R G B mask env phase
# Audio : A time freq pan vol mod ch freqR waveType duty env phase attack jitter depth

# --- Ramp-in (00:00-00:15): both banks ease up together ---
0 40 50 >0 255 140 0 10 0 0                  # AMBER bank, phase 0,   bright 0 -> 20
0 40 50 >0 0 120 255 5 0 180                 # BLUE  bank, phase 180, bright 0 -> 20
A 0 10000 0 >0 40 1 0 0 4 0 0 0 0 100        # ch1 GENUS click: 10 kHz carrier, 40 Hz square
                                             # gate, 4% duty, full depth. `attack` is written
                                             # 0 because env 0 ignores it; the sharp edge is
                                             # the point — GENUS specifies a 1 ms click train,
                                             # and 4% of a 25 ms period IS 1 ms.
15000 40 50 20 255 140 0 10 0 0              # amber at the 20% cap
15000 40 50 20 0 120 255 5 0 180             # blue matched to it => luminance ~flat
A 30000 10000 0 45 40 1 0 0 4 0 0 0 0 100    # click settled at vol 45

# --- Hold, fixed 40 Hz, ~14 min (00:30-14:30) ---
#   Nothing moves. GENUS efficacy depends on a FIXED 40 Hz: no frequency LFO and
#   no anti-habituation drift here, unlike the slower sessions.

# --- Ramp-out (14:30-15:00): both banks and the click fade together ---
870000 40 50 >20 255 140 0 10 0 0
870000 40 50 >20 0 120 255 5 0 180
A 870000 10000 0 >45 40 1 0 0 4 0 0 0 0 100
900000 40 50 0 255 140 0 10 0 0
900000 40 50 0 0 120 255 5 0 180
A 900000 10000 0 0 40 1 0 0 4 0 0 0 0 100
